  "summary": "whalibmob 5.33.30: static patterns match in library modules without traced installer-harm behavior",
  "details": "Pattern matches fire on several files in lib/: MediaService.js imports fs/http/https and performs fs.readFileSync and https.request calls; Registration.js contains repeated 'ping' tokens; WebVersion.js references 'curl' alongside https.get and 'ps' tokens; socks.js references 'curl', a POST, and 'hostname'. These are keyword co-occurrences in a package whose name resembles established library packages, and no specific installer-side data read is tied to a specific non-first-party destination. No lifecycle scripts, obfuscated droppers, env/credential path reads (such as ~/.aws, ~/.ssh, ~/.npmrc), browser or wallet store access, or hardcoded attacker C2 endpoints are observed in the cited evidence. The pattern shape alone is not sufficient to characterize this as exfiltration, remote code execution, or a backdoor.",
